{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbVRH9HHPPARRXqckFnw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES\n\nP2 tests/live.rs — acceptance criterion 4 is not met. The PR has no opt-in live pi test, so nothing does a real round trip or saves a fresh pi fixture. `tests/live.rs` is cursor only and isn't in the PR's file list. Fix: add an `#[ignore]` pi test that runs one real `pi -p --mode json` call and writes the raw stdout to `tests/fixtures/pi/`.\n\nP2 src/backends/pi/mod.rs:276 — `session_id` comes only from pi's `session` header. If the header is missing (truncated stream, or pi not echoing it), the record has no session id and resume breaks. The id was chosen before launch, so nothing should depend on the echo. Fix: have `finish` fall back to the minted id, or have the caller store it.\n\nP3 src/backends/pi/mod.rs:136-216 — `handle_line` repeats the same `usage.get(..).and_then(as_f64).filter(is_finite).unwrap_or(0.0)` chain five times. Fix: use a small `num(usage, key)` helper.\n\nP3 src/backends/pi/mod.rs:145 — the `.is_none()` early return is redundant, because the `match` below already falls through to `_ => false`. Fix: delete it.\n\nP3 src/backends/pi/mod.rs:265 — `agent_end` with no assistant message sets `is_error: Some(false)` and returns the last `message_end` text. That reads as success when pi gave no result. Fix: treat a missing assistant message as an error.\n\nI checked against AC1 (parser fixtures: answer, tool calls, resume, error), AC2 (run/resume/cancel/watch through a fake pi, with `watch` used inside `wait_terminal`) and AC3 (read-only rejected). They look covered. I did not run the tests.\n\nSTATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":61062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":641,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ef50a4c-f74f-4f52-8bd2-15d5ae30bbdf","uuid":"28dd3f9b-2375-4677-9eb0-2bb64eb97782","timestamp":"2026-10-01T12:08:22.545Z","request_id":"req_011CfbVRGgWNYbHKqaWnTEx4"}
